1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,600
This is Press.

2
00:00:02,820 --> 00:00:04,720
One phone keeps score for the whole

3
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:10,100
group — skins, Nassau, Wolf, the lot

4
00:00:10,780 --> 00:00:12,800
— and it does the math while

5
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:14,560
you play.

6
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:17,700
No account, no app store, nothing to

7
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:18,300
install.

8
00:00:19,380 --> 00:00:21,520
Here's a full round in four minutes.

9
00:00:24,580 --> 00:00:27,280
Start New Round, and type everyone in.

10
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:30,400
The handicap goes in the box beside

11
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:32,420
the name — that's what every net

12
00:00:32,420 --> 00:00:33,960
score in the round comes off.

13
00:00:34,780 --> 00:00:37,140
Press remembers your regular crew, so next

14
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:38,860
week this is one tap.

15
00:00:40,547 --> 00:00:43,607
Open Course. Search for it and Press

16
00:00:43,607 --> 00:00:45,227
pulls in the pars and the stroke

17
00:00:45,227 --> 00:00:47,947
indexes, or load one you saved earlier.

18
00:00:48,767 --> 00:00:50,567
Either way the card opens right here —

19
00:00:50,567 --> 00:00:52,967
and search data gets read before you

20
00:00:52,967 --> 00:00:55,047
see it, so anything that looks off

21
00:00:55,047 --> 00:00:57,647
is flagged. Check it against the real

22
00:00:57,647 --> 00:00:59,847
card once, then save it.

23
00:00:59,847 --> 00:01:04,827
Everything downstream — every stroke anybody gets — comes

24
00:01:04,827 --> 00:01:06,247
off these eighteen numbers.

25
00:01:08,007 --> 00:01:10,167
Games is where the money starts.

26
00:01:11,147 --> 00:01:12,047
Tap what you're playing.

27
00:01:13,067 --> 00:01:15,607
Every format carries its own rules behind

28
00:01:15,607 --> 00:01:18,687
the info button — so when somebody at

29
00:01:18,687 --> 00:01:20,767
the table has never played Wolf, you

30
00:01:20,767 --> 00:01:21,987
don't have to be the one who

31
00:01:21,987 --> 00:01:22,647
explains it.

32
00:01:24,194 --> 00:01:25,234
The full list:

33
00:01:25,994 --> 00:01:29,334
stroke play, match play — singles or

34
00:01:29,334 --> 00:01:33,354
two-man best ball — skins, Stableford, Wolf,

35
00:01:33,814 --> 00:01:36,994
Vegas with the birdie flip, Quota, Nassau

36
00:01:36,994 --> 00:01:39,994
with presses, and a Thursday-night league format.

37
00:01:41,114 --> 00:01:43,114
Net runs through all of it:

38
00:01:43,814 --> 00:01:46,114
one stroke per hole down the stroke

39
00:01:46,114 --> 00:01:48,714
index, and a second on the hardest

40
00:01:48,714 --> 00:01:51,274
holes when somebody's playing off more than

41
00:01:51,274 --> 00:01:51,874
eighteen.

42
00:01:53,394 --> 00:01:55,514
Money sets the stake per game.

43
00:01:56,354 --> 00:01:58,014
Five a skin, twenty on the Nassau.

44
00:01:58,014 --> 00:02:01,234
Leave it blank and you're playing for

45
00:02:01,234 --> 00:02:03,714
nothing — and you can change it

46
00:02:03,714 --> 00:02:04,574
mid-round from the Board.

47
00:02:06,264 --> 00:02:09,444
Start Round, and this is where you

48
00:02:09,444 --> 00:02:11,864
live for the next four hours.

49
00:02:13,024 --> 00:02:16,924
Hole number, par, one row per player.

50
00:02:18,044 --> 00:02:18,664
Tap the score.

51
00:02:19,844 --> 00:02:21,524
Par is the chip in the middle,

52
00:02:22,184 --> 00:02:24,904
and the dots beside a name are

53
00:02:24,904 --> 00:02:26,604
the strokes they're getting on this hole.

54
00:02:28,264 --> 00:02:30,424
The line at the top is the

55
00:02:30,424 --> 00:02:33,084
money, live, all round.

56
00:02:34,144 --> 00:02:36,144
Close out a hole and it tells

57
00:02:36,144 --> 00:02:39,164
you exactly what just changed hands, and

58
00:02:39,164 --> 00:02:40,144
who it came from.

59
00:02:41,534 --> 00:02:45,234
Greenies, sandies, barkies — claim them on

60
00:02:45,234 --> 00:02:47,014
the hole and they land on the

61
00:02:47,694 --> 00:02:49,014
card, priced.

62
00:02:49,014 --> 00:02:51,284
Wolf picks its partner right here, before

63
00:02:51,294 --> 00:02:52,094
anybody's hit.

64
00:02:52,974 --> 00:02:54,014
Nassau presses too:

65
00:02:54,754 --> 00:02:56,654
take one by hand, or set it

66
00:02:56,654 --> 00:02:58,714
to press automatically when a side goes

67
00:02:58,714 --> 00:02:59,394
two down.

68
00:03:01,014 --> 00:03:03,154
The Board tab is every game at

69
00:03:03,154 --> 00:03:05,074
once — who's up in the match,

70
00:03:05,294 --> 00:03:07,994
who's holding skins, where the money actually

71
00:03:07,994 --> 00:03:08,594
sits.

72
00:03:09,454 --> 00:03:11,254
Somebody gave you the wrong handicap on

73
00:03:11,254 --> 00:03:11,854
the first tee?

74
00:03:12,474 --> 00:03:14,694
Fix it here, and every board behind

75
00:03:14,694 --> 00:03:15,834
it recalculates.

76
00:03:17,481 --> 00:03:19,861
Card is the whole scorecard, eighteen across.

77
00:03:19,861 --> 00:03:23,241
Tap a number to fix it, tap

78
00:03:23,241 --> 00:03:24,961
a hole to jump straight back to

79
00:03:24,961 --> 00:03:25,561
it.

80
00:03:26,661 --> 00:03:29,121
Finish the round and Press settles it.

81
00:03:29,121 --> 00:03:32,641
Winner up top, then the superlatives —

82
00:03:32,641 --> 00:03:36,501
Shot of the Day, The Snowman, The

83
00:03:36,501 --> 00:03:42,081
ATM, Sandbagger — and each one cites

84
00:03:42,081 --> 00:03:44,131
the number it's based on, so the

85
00:03:44,141 --> 00:03:47,741
argument is short.

86
00:03:49,621 --> 00:03:51,921
Then the bit that normally takes ten

87
00:03:51,921 --> 00:03:53,061
minutes in the car park.

88
00:03:53,901 --> 00:03:56,661
Press resolves the whole group into the

89
00:03:56,661 --> 00:04:00,241
fewest payments that settle it.

90
00:04:00,241 --> 00:04:02,061
Three people pay, not twelve.

91
00:04:03,761 --> 00:04:05,921
Share gives you the scoreboard as an

92
00:04:05,921 --> 00:04:08,421
image, or the full card as an

93
00:04:08,421 --> 00:04:11,301
image — both straight into the group chat.

94
00:04:13,031 --> 00:04:14,971
And underneath, the round itself.

95
00:04:16,031 --> 00:04:18,151
The whole thing is packed into the

96
00:04:18,151 --> 00:04:20,901
link — point another phone's camera at

97
00:04:20,911 --> 00:04:22,331
the code and it opens in their

98
00:04:22,331 --> 00:04:23,171
copy of Press.

99
00:04:24,131 --> 00:04:25,051
Nothing is uploaded.

100
00:04:26,111 --> 00:04:27,491
No server ever sees it.

101
00:04:30,731 --> 00:04:33,671
On their phone it arrives held —

102
00:04:33,671 --> 00:04:35,851
sent to you, not saved — until

103
00:04:35,851 --> 00:04:37,671
they tap Keep it.

104
00:04:38,071 --> 00:04:39,931
Mid-round, the same link hands the card

105
00:04:40,231 --> 00:04:42,211
over and they carry on scoring from

106
00:04:42,211 --> 00:04:43,651
where you stopped.

107
00:04:43,651 --> 00:04:45,551
And if you both end up keeping

108
00:04:46,191 --> 00:04:48,231
score, Press puts the two cards side

109
00:04:48,231 --> 00:04:51,411
by side and asks which one is

110
00:04:51,411 --> 00:04:52,011
real.

111
00:04:53,411 --> 00:04:54,551
Which brings us to the thing that

112
00:04:54,551 --> 00:04:56,311
actually matters out on the course.

113
00:04:57,131 --> 00:04:57,731
Watch:

114
00:04:58,071 --> 00:04:59,531
I'm killing the network completely.

115
00:05:00,431 --> 00:05:01,031
Reload.

116
00:05:01,651 --> 00:05:03,151
Still there, still scoring.

117
00:05:04,331 --> 00:05:06,871
Every round, every saved course, every bit

118
00:05:06,871 --> 00:05:08,691
of history lives on your phone.

119
00:05:08,691 --> 00:05:12,191
That's the privacy story too — there's

120
00:05:12,191 --> 00:05:14,231
no account to make, and nothing to

121
00:05:14,231 --> 00:05:14,831
leak.

122
00:05:16,081 --> 00:05:17,661
Add it to your home screen and

123
00:05:17,661 --> 00:05:19,641
it opens like anything else on your

124
00:05:20,341 --> 00:05:20,471
phone.

125
00:05:20,481 --> 00:05:24,721
It's free, it's at pressgolf.netlify.app, and the

126
00:05:24,721 --> 00:05:25,461
link's in the description.

127
00:05:25,461 --> 00:05:27,701
Now go take their money.
